<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9629] JDBCv2: JdbcResultSet must support types conversions</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9629</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Now &lt;tt&gt;JdbcResultSet&lt;/tt&gt; doesn&apos;t support data types transformation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;e.g.: if the attribute type is SHORT&lt;br/&gt;
all the methods below must return valid value::&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;getByte, getShort, getInt, getLong, getFloat, getDouble, getBigDecimal, getBoolean, getString, getNString&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See the table B-6 at the JDBC spec  (see also &lt;a href=&quot;http://docs.oracle.com/javase/6/docs/technotes/guides/jdbc/getstart/mapping.html#996857&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;8.9.5 and 8.9.6&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
